## ✅ File Structure (Upload All of These)

```
Training-Portal/
├── index.html        ← Main HTML page (required)
├── _redirects        ← Netlify SPA routing (required)
├── netlify.toml      ← Netlify build config (required)
├── README.md         ← This file
└── src/
    ├── app.js        ← All JavaScript, routing, Stripe logic
    └── style.css     ← All styles
```

---

## 🔌 How to Activate Stripe Payments

### Step 1 — Create Your Stripe Payment Links

Go to [dashboard.stripe.com](https://dashboard.stripe.com) and create **4 Payment Links**:

| Product | Description | After-Payment URL |
|---|---|---|
| Full Certificate Program | All 6 modules | https://reflectionsofgracebiblestudies.netlify.app/#/success |
| Module 3 — Counseling | Integrated Christian Counseling | https://reflectionsofgracebiblestudies.netlify.app/#/success |
| Module 6 — Gen X | Generation X Left the Church | https://reflectionsofgracebiblestudies.netlify.app/#/success |
| Ministry Donation | One-time or recurring gift | https://reflectionsofgracebiblestudies.netlify.app/#/success |

### Step 2 — Get Your Publishable Key

In Stripe Dashboard → Developers → API Keys → copy your **Publishable key** (starts with `pk_live_`)

### Step 3 — Update src/app.js

Open `src/app.js` and find the `STRIPE_CONFIG` block at the top. Replace the placeholder values:

```javascript
const STRIPE_CONFIG = {
  publishableKey: "pk_live_YOUR_ACTUAL_KEY_HERE",
  links: {
    full:       "https://buy.stripe.com/YOUR_ACTUAL_FULL_LINK",
    counseling: "https://buy.stripe.com/YOUR_ACTUAL_COUNSELING_LINK",
    genx:       "https://buy.stripe.com/YOUR_ACTUAL_GENX_LINK",
    donate:     "https://buy.stripe.com/YOUR_ACTUAL_DONATE_LINK",
  }
};
```

### Step 4 — Commit and Deploy

Commit the updated `src/app.js` to GitHub. Netlify will automatically redeploy in 60–90 seconds.

---

## 🚀 Netlify Setup

Make sure your Netlify site is connected to this repository:

1. Go to [app.netlify.com](https://app.netlify.com)
2. Site → Site Settings → Build & Deploy → Link repository
3. Select: `rograceoutreach-a11y/Training-Portal`
4. Build command: *(leave blank)*
5. Publish directory: `.` (a single dot — the root)
6. Save → Trigger deploy

